{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CL9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\gamma$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\gamma$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-definition-dotted-arrows}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-cat-dotted-arrows-independent}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-cat-dotted-arrows-base-change}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fbda97e4e1cae5b738715b07c2247575583d983da0f857e803d61a67b1c2fef9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:60c5e8f1406c7d527e657b2ce747d04a9835f3de52f5f6602ab10b46a3fd6f4a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe preceding definition is a special case of Categories, \nDefinition <REF_0001>.\nThe category of dotted arrows depends on <MATH_0001> in general.\nIf <MATH_0002> is representable by an algebraic space\n(or if automorphism groups of objects over fields are trivial), then\nof course there is at most one <MATH_0003> and one does not need\nto check the commutativity of the triangle. More generally, we\nhave Lemma <REF_0002>.\nThe commutativity of the triangle is important in the proof\nof compatibility with base change, see\nproof of Lemma <REF_0003>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:884a0bae55f02c18809155245b0179d3e54ed931ee23c997aa9f4e1707beeb6c", "unit_id": "tag:0CL9:prose-0002"}
